  "rate": "-3%",
  "parts": [
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "11",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p11-jenny-explainer-first",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777",
        "2": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p11-jenny-s01-c1-d2eb8c2423ba",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Suppose an app stores logos but also needs to update orders. Reading a logo by key fits S three. Updating related order records together asks for transaction semantics instead. Start with the operation, not the storage price.",
          "text_sha256": "d2eb8c2423babe2653a61631c9ece9f911a14b26a5d3e95b1e5fe2797d86560b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4b131338000b094622fd082468c29b768194768b00f395ba74b0cd3d0895e2d5",
          "asset_sha256": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p11-jenny-s01-c2-44d5a1bcd884",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Now check how quickly the data must be read or restored, how long it stays, and where copies may live. A cheap archive can fail the recovery deadline. Include retrieval and replication costs as well as storage.",
          "text_sha256": "44d5a1bcd88485fd18f66e01c035ad1fbef876d494243d0bd2f99c2c562f0acd",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "44d5a1bcd88485fd18f66e01c035ad1fbef876d494243d0bd2f99c2c562f0acd",
          "asset_sha256": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p11-jenny-s01-c3-9f0a8d258a1e",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Now follow one request all the way through. The right object can still fail to reach the app if the identity cannot use the key, the network path is broken, or the index has not caught up. Test and observe the complete path.",
          "text_sha256": "9f0a8d258a1e4bfc262371d16b45a8acee7b16a4ef97e30ee6879186c127ca74",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9f0a8d258a1e4bfc262371d16b45a8acee7b16a4ef97e30ee6879186c127ca74",
          "asset_sha256": "6776d22ed6ace6943e381db67f263606ad64b95c5dc50c4ddec156f618f21777"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p11-jenny-s02-c1-8ec16ed71247",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "The first origin is a web fleet serving its own files. The fleet still needs patching and scaling. Instance store is temporary; EBS persists independently when configured to do so, but the volume belongs to one Availability Zone.",
          "text_sha256": "8ec16ed7124793b1fe3bbe436c95d6229744bff7237d3c819279c1b8be1fca18",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "8ec16ed7124793b1fe3bbe436c95d6229744bff7237d3c819279c1b8be1fca18",
          "asset_sha256": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p11-jenny-s02-c2-96c85e6ea945",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "If multiple web servers need to see the same files, EFS gives them a shared Linux namespace. Changing a file once can be enough for the fleet; you still operate the web servers and need a resilient file layer.",
          "text_sha256": "96c85e6ea945b029cc4c9a93b9a591606f4dbf451efc697e2ab0747b32a7b246",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "96c85e6ea945b029cc4c9a93b9a591606f4dbf451efc697e2ab0747b32a7b246",
          "asset_sha256": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p11-jenny-s02-c3-7bef5f58db0c",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For a static logo, CloudFront can read it from a private S three origin and return it without asking an application server to run. Keep the separate compute path for requests that need application logic.",
          "text_sha256": "7bef5f58db0cc60c39341f2d74075d4c4f2e383d2a4832f576c2d6cd72955d72",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "f223bc27df53b5c89d58dcbef0ec11450d398db9314cd3cac3c0daf55c11323a",
          "asset_sha256": "896ac848505c7ea9a31bf66d61be34d7a92cf10070f9d41bcabe51c33be07bbe"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "module": "09",
      "part": "12",
      "revision": "2026-11-24-m09p12-jenny-explainer-first",
      "approved_assets": {
        "1": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b",
        "2": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18",
        "3": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f",
        "4": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
      },
      "units": [
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s01-c1-5da0502987fe",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Learn why a global S three endpoint alone cannot deliver regional recovery. The client calls one Multi-Region Access Point instead of selecting a Regional endpoint.",
          "text_sha256": "5da0502987fe975ec8eda2897601483cd44271a1a44549ab6409b3a30d988cee",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "315860f5332cfb71d28a9a44b9fe024ab20ceb47f02b138f67252f4cbc520a59",
          "asset_sha256": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s01-c2-bb41f447f28f",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Imagine the client is routed to Region B, but the object was written only in Region A. The new route cannot create the missing data. Replication or a separate write must put the object there before the read can succeed.",
          "text_sha256": "bb41f447f28f5d64d2ca4f34a4fc8d0719579ac987b316aa8e0e0e2e044190f1",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "bb41f447f28f5d64d2ca4f34a4fc8d0719579ac987b316aa8e0e0e2e044190f1",
          "asset_sha256": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s01-c3-392a6f3a8e81",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Check the access point and bucket policies, object ownership, and key permissions when encryption requires them. A working global endpoint does not prove the routed request is authorized.",
          "text_sha256": "392a6f3a8e81847c823fe6b6846a720c4b031fff7ba93f8a276d41e605b6e540",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "392a6f3a8e81847c823fe6b6846a720c4b031fff7ba93f8a276d41e605b6e540",
          "asset_sha256": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s01-c4-82590a3aac93",
          "slide": 1,
          "text": "Before shifting traffic with failover controls, verify that the destination has the data and permits the read. Test that request end to end.",
          "text_sha256": "82590a3aac93c1123616c1f8050a083e0b4109a54ce4f393cd6455e6d53c6db4",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "82590a3aac93c1123616c1f8050a083e0b4109a54ce4f393cd6455e6d53c6db4",
          "asset_sha256": "b5018a2021842e3a76b91a787137b1c1215d633341e083cbc424288ae600342b"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s02-c1-b62f1d1a4269",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "In this older pattern the client reads a stored object through S three Object Lambda. A function changes what goes back to that client, such as converting the response, without having to replace the stored object.",
          "text_sha256": "b62f1d1a426979f69c3950d12b6366b98af515e38d25135a16c4eb333ca66419",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "c3d9dfbe58b3695ecccaab70cc23fad1af1cdaf4a5fbfd64d02419f6b9d29dcc",
          "asset_sha256": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s02-c2-be8676b70bce",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Since November seventh, twenty twenty-five, S three Object Lambda is limited to existing users and select A W S partners. For a new design, consider transformation in the application, an API, or a suitable CloudFront solution.",
          "text_sha256": "be8676b70bce33d3562ac35d888ec19cbf95c321ccf2770b0a30b0b519ff311a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "ef529d46d68d0c96780bf4383f6a69294fff975975e0a5cfb98a95382da9a220",
          "asset_sha256": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s02-c3-bc7ae8683d8d",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "Glacier vault-service Vault Lock is a retention control for the older vault API. It is not the control you apply to an ordinary S three bucket object.",
          "text_sha256": "bc7ae8683d8d1f78a1aee9e8d00cc7ed11d1ccd73ef5cf32766042cc5046fddb",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "09fa13a96d8a1c4e7d9276a0acd5fbdaa5a5f1f702fa2a2e8124b4e62bdeb604",
          "asset_sha256": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s02-c4-e91bfbe526eb",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "For protected versions in an S three bucket, use S three Object Lock retention or legal hold according to the requirement.",
          "text_sha256": "e91bfbe526eb1e7047ac310a0d96e5f0805bc853a93bfd6aa141bb54f644c15a",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "32f04cde105b76732871b9283c382c8f41abf489417d9bbe4b200e12355c99cd",
          "asset_sha256": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s02-c5-42b5482f4568",
          "slide": 2,
          "text": "A Glacier storage class controls storage and retrieval characteristics. Choosing it does not, by itself, prevent an authorized deletion.",
          "text_sha256": "42b5482f456816be10b12bdac2bcac820042617f6179ad52656497aa8b740e46",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "42b5482f456816be10b12bdac2bcac820042617f6179ad52656497aa8b740e46",
          "asset_sha256": "1e7480d8c1c5a2e7c010a0384721b63e3f1129359ac0b7aa2329d4a43171ce18"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s03-c1-dd35700fcd82",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The application signs one operation against a bucket and key and specifies an expiry and any required signed headers. Use a presigned get for a read or a presigned put for the intended upload.",
          "text_sha256": "dd35700fcd8295d43ef45737aff0dca61d94f16bdb1c9374b15176d9674e68ba",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "9e3218516344da97d64e92cf25b1b1d2b5da7eb85b8967c6982c46e249b8c4ae",
          "asset_sha256": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s03-c2-ef48ee6b531b",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The client sends the signed request directly to S three. The signature grants that request without handing over the signer’s A W S credentials. Whoever holds the URL can use it while it remains valid, so protect the link.",
          "text_sha256": "ef48ee6b531bdc5b0d30b3fe4ced030333e5e90acf29023e40ebe0059305ebb2",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "a6c53dc3dfe40d8f44d149477a3d8e5a42c175d14709b27c3f97b0b16fcdd444",
          "asset_sha256": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s03-c3-e4b59e723289",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "The usable lifetime cannot outlast the signing credentials. A link signed by a temporary role session can stop working before the expiry time printed in the link.",
          "text_sha256": "e4b59e7232891c63569ca077825799ce1985e2dc78d2e48a5195df9de21ac836",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "e4b59e7232891c63569ca077825799ce1985e2dc78d2e48a5195df9de21ac836",
          "asset_sha256": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s03-c4-91519b2733ef",
          "slide": 3,
          "text": "For uploads, verify the resulting object and its size or checksum as appropriate. An expiring link does not validate the file.",
          "text_sha256": "91519b2733efbab2b26baa1ef0ae397977b84566f836e700416b21471515823b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "91519b2733efbab2b26baa1ef0ae397977b84566f836e700416b21471515823b",
          "asset_sha256": "8e7c93ad58316117adf9dab74ffbeef18a5b5c253346c1ba150c5c79e9606b0f"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s04-c1-b9f670285fd7",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Use server access logs when you need supported request details delivered to a logging bucket. Delivery is not real-time tracing; verify the logs arrive before relying on them for an investigation.",
          "text_sha256": "b9f670285fd71f5c17b1c4ea3ea51324afeaf0adbc44519dc18f8d6271a5901c",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "b9f670285fd71f5c17b1c4ea3ea51324afeaf0adbc44519dc18f8d6271a5901c",
          "asset_sha256": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s04-c2-b5b30422aa72",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "To learn who called an object API, enable CloudTrail S three data events for the operations and resources in scope. Then look for the caller on the matching record. Management-event history alone does not answer that question.",
          "text_sha256": "b5b30422aa72ccdf4bca010f6568b6f30ca72be97746f163a46be867ee635c0b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "4bef6c3a9036f6d4c3a24463e98dd80e7ee7731fa4b8a32782824a860982ec2a",
          "asset_sha256": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
        },
        {
          "id": "m09p12-jenny-s04-c3-20e29b9001a0",
          "slide": 4,
          "text": "Use request metrics or Storage Lens when the question is what trend changed. Their scope and cadence differ. Neither substitutes for an individual object API audit record.",
          "text_sha256": "20e29b9001a00d102a4d7f4bd22733baf6da14dd811c3f09099d90c9bb2bc90b",
          "canonical_text_sha256": "20e29b9001a00d102a4d7f4bd22733baf6da14dd811c3f09099d90c9bb2bc90b",
          "asset_sha256": "f0fb79afa233ee0df806a60fbb013e95237456d6b720f46a91e365448acc914c"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
